# @flag --add-user                              Create a user provisioner certificate used to create a new user
# @flag --host                                  Create a host certificate instead of a user certificate
# @option --host-id <UUID>                      Specify a UUID to identify the host rather than using an auto-generated UUID
# @option --password-file <file>                The path to the file containing the password to encrypt the private key
# @option --principal -n* <name>                Add the specified principal (user or host names) to the certificate request
# @option --private-key <value>                 When signing an existing public key, use this flag to specify the corresponding private key so that the pair can be added to an SSH Agent
# @option --provisioner-password-file <file>    The path to the file containing the password to decrypt the one-time token generating key
